{
  "name": "MAIN - 2-Pass Upscale (pick 2 sub workflows)",
  "author": "Pfannkuchensack",
  "description": "Parent workflow: generate at base resolution, then upscale + refine. Each pass has its own model type and its own settings.",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "contact": "",
  "tags": "main, parent, upscale, callable",
  "notes": "Pfannkuchensacks Workflow Package\n\nEverything is pre-filled. The two things you normally touch are the\n\"Saved Workflow\" pickers:\n\n  Pass 1  ->  any  \"TXT2IMG - <model>\"\n  Pass 2  ->  any  \"UPSCALE REFINE - <model>\"\n\nThe two passes may use DIFFERENT model types, e.g. Krea-2 for the text-to-image\npass and SDXL for the refine. That is why prompt, negative prompt, steps and CFG\nexist separately for each pass: those values are model-specific and a shared\nvalue would force a bad compromise. Krea-2-Turbo wants 8 steps at CFG 1.0 and\nignores the negative prompt entirely; SDXL wants ~30 steps at CFG 5-8 and does\nuse it; FLUX wants ~25 steps at guidance ~3.5.\n\nShared on purpose: base resolution, scale and seed. Those are properties of the\npicture you are making, not of the model.\n\nThe model itself is selected INSIDE each sub workflow and appears here as an\nextra field on the call node once a workflow is picked.\n\nPass 2 renders at Base Width/Height x Scale. Keep base dimensions a multiple of\n16 so the scaled size stays valid for every model type.\n\nSeed is randomised per run and shared by both passes. Swap the Random Integer\nnode for a plain Integer node if you want reproducible output.",
